:"2025-04-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CO"},{"bioguideId":"S000344","fullName":"Rep. Sherman, Brad [D-CA-32]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:39:02+00:00","id":"hr1159-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-10","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"1159","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Transportation and Public Works","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001285","district":26,"fullName":"Rep. Brownley, Julia [D-CA-26]","party":"D","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-10","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Honoring Our Fallen TSA Officers Act</strong></p><p>This bill includes Transportation Security Administration (TSA) employees in the&nbsp;Public Safety Officers' Benefits (PSOB) program under certain conditions. Specifically, the bill&nbsp;extends PSOB program&nbsp;death and disability benefits&nbsp;to TSA employees performing official duties related to protecting the nation's transportation systems.</p><p>As background, the PSOB program provides cash benefits to federal, state, and local law enforcement officers; firefighters; employees of emergency management agencies; and members of emergency medical services agencies who are killed or permanently and totally disabled as the result of personal injuries sustained in the line of duty.&nbsp;PSOB death benefits are payable to the eligible spouse and children of a public safety officer.&nbsp;Further, the Public Safety Officers’ Educational Assistance&nbsp;program, a component of the PSOB program, provides higher-education assistance to the children and spouses of public safety officers who are eligible for PSOB death or disability benefits.&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-09T15:27:23Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Honoring Our Fallen TSA Officers Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2025-10-25T08:05:39Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-10-25T08:05:39Z"}
